                <pb facs="0123" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G/309: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-30T18:00:00-04:00">October 30, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 30—5:19 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. On Saturday efforts were made by Argentina to interest Chile, Peru, and
                    Brazil in backing a move to postpone the Conference for 3 months. Argentina
                    urged postponement because of unliquidated Chaco, Leticia, and Cuban situations.
                    Chile is awaiting indication of Peruvian attitude before taking any action but
                    sees no gain in delay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
